<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Macadams yr shr, div soar.</title>
<headline>Macadams yr shr, div soar.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>		 (million of rand unless indicated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)	  55.7	vs 33.5</p>
<p>    Yr div	     16.0	vs  5.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income    10.66     vs  5.89</p>
<p>    Pre-tax	    16.36     vs  7.50</p>
<p>    Tax		   5.70     vs  1.61</p>
<p>    Interest paid     2.27     vs  1.07</p>
<p>    Turnover	  125.40     vs 79.11</p>
<p>Div payment to be advised</p>
<p>on register April 11</p>
<p>Full name: Macadams Manufacturing (bakery equipment manufacturer)</p>
<p>NOTE: Shareholders will be offered capitalisation shares in lieu of the dividend in the ratio of two new shares for every 100 held.</p>
<p>The group said that the joint venture agreement signed last year with three international partners was expected to further boost the demand for its ovens, especially in export markets. It was therefore confident of continued higher profitability in the current year.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
